[Q-C] SUCCESS RATE -- is it the same every time?
  convergence rate (R = 1.000 at ep 4000) : 146/200 = 73.0%
    Wilson 95% CI          : [66.5%, 78.7%]   (half-width 6.1 pp)
    Clopper-Pearson 95% CI : [66.3%, 79.0%]  (exact, conservative)
  mean greedy team reward : 0.9613  bootstrap 95% CI [0.9519, 0.9706]   (sd 0.0679)
  reward-band distribution (every run falls in a discrete band, never in between):
      perfect (1.000)         : 146/200 =  73.0%   Wilson 95% CI [66.5%, 78.7%]
      joint-channel (0.875)   :  46/200 =  23.0%   Wilson 95% CI [17.7%, 29.3%]
      single-bit (0.750)      :   8/200 =   4.0%   Wilson 95% CI [2.0%, 7.7%]
      floor (0.500)           :   0/200 =   0.0%   Wilson 95% CI [0.0%, 1.9%]
  block reproducibility: seeds split into 5 independent, disjoint blocks
      block 0 (seeds    0-39):  27/40 =  67.5%  [52.0%, 79.9%]
      block 1 (seeds   40-79):  30/40 =  75.0%  [59.8%, 85.8%]
      block 2 (seeds  80-119):  31/40 =  77.5%  [62.5%, 87.7%]
      block 3 (seeds 120-159):  31/40 =  77.5%  [62.5%, 87.7%]
      block 4 (seeds 160-199):  27/40 =  67.5%  [52.0%, 79.9%]
    H0_C1: the convergence rate is the same in every block
      permutation chi2 = 2.131, p = 0.7315  -> fail to reject H0  (rate spread across blocks: 68%-78%)
  lock-in episode (final convention held from here to ep 4000), perfect runs:
      median 2000  bootstrap 95% CI [2000, 2250]  IQR [1750, 2500]  range [750, 4000]
  stability 4000->6000 (perfect runs keeping the SAME convention at every snapshot): 146/146  Wilson [97.4%, 100.0%]
  non-perfect runs at ep 4000: 54;  became perfect by ep 6000: 13;  frozen in the same imperfect convention: 13/54

